---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { site } from '../site';
---

<Base title="Support" description="How Furlough works, the one way out, and what to do if a shield seems stuck.">
  <section class="wrap page">
    <header class="head" data-reveal>
      <div class="eyebrow amber">Support</div>
      <h1 class="display">If you need out, the way out is Apple's.</h1>
      <p class="sub">Furlough for iPhone</p>
    </header>

    <article class="card prose body" data-reveal style="--d: .1s">
      <p>Furlough shields the apps and websites you choose outside the hours you allowed them, and holds any change that would give you more time until a delay you set in advance has passed.</p>

      <div class="note">
        <p><strong>There is no unblock button, and that is deliberate.</strong> If it could be undone the moment you wanted it undone, it would not be doing anything.</p>
        <p>Two things do forgive a mistake: your first week caps a loosening's wait at an hour, and for fifteen minutes after a tightening takes effect the editor will put it back exactly as it was. Neither is an unblock — the only thing either can hand back is the state you were already in. <a href="/help/windows-and-budgets/">Both are explained here</a>.</p>
      </div>

      <h2>If you need out</h2>
      <p>The way out is Apple's, not ours, and it always works: <span class="path">Settings › Screen Time › Apps with Screen Time Access › Furlough › off.</span> Every shield lifts immediately and app deletion is re-enabled. Your rules are kept: turn access back on and Furlough picks up where it left off.</p>

      <h2>If a shield seems stuck</h2>
      <ol>
        <li>Open Furlough and tap <span class="path">Settings › Re-apply enforcement now</span>. This re-registers every schedule and re-applies shields from saved state.</li>
        <li>Check <span class="path">Settings › Activity log</span> to see what Furlough has been doing.</li>
        <li>If that does not help, use the Screen Time switch above, then turn it back on.</li>
      </ol>

      <h2>Things worth knowing</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Windows must be at least 15 minutes. A night that runs past midnight is kept as two windows, one either side of it, and each half needs its own fifteen.</li>
        <li>An app cannot be deleted while it is shielded. That is intentional, and the Screen Time switch above releases it.</li>
        <li>Moving your iPhone's clock forward does not buy time: queued changes are held while the clock runs ahead, and released when it is set back.</li>
        <li>The Anchor needs an NFC tag you have paired. Everything else works without one; <a href="/help/nfc-tags/">which tag to get and where to keep it</a> is its own page.</li>
        <li>Apple's Screen Time API does not exist on the Mac. Furlough for Mac enforces on its own and is open source: <a href={site.githubURL} rel="noopener">build it from GitHub</a>.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Still stuck?</h2>
      <p>Email <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a> with what you were doing and what happened. The activity log in Settings is the most useful thing to describe.</p>

      <p class="contact"><a href="/privacy/">Privacy policy</a></p>
    </article>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  .page { padding: clamp(24px, 6vh, 64px) 0 0; max-width: 760px; }
  .head h1 { margin-top: 12px; font-size: clamp(34px, 5vw, 56px); }
  .sub { color: var(--faint); font-size: 14px; margin-top: 14px; }
  .body { margin-top: 28px; padding: clamp(22px, 4vw, 36px); }
  .contact { margin-top: 32px; padding-top: 18px; border-top: 1px solid var(--edge); font-size: 14px; }
</style>
